 but someone let him drive knowing he was  impaired  despite having a record of drug abuse he  was able to hold down a job driving a  truck  he was not merely driving himself home  at night  from a night out nor getting to work  while still under the influence the  morning after  he was driving a vehicle of 26 000  pounds that became a lethal weapon  how is that possible  nevada's a gaming state as a casino  employee  you're required to have a gaming license  a dui impacts your ability to attain  that license  and would result in a possible loss of  employment  this same philosophy should apply to  drivers  cruise line employees may be hired for  multiple roles across the ship  whether it be as a member of the  entertainment team or a chef  or an electrician yet for every employee  the number one priority is onboard  safety  and they are all trained to help  evacuate the ship  and as part of their safety requirements  crew are not permitted to be under the  influence at any time when they're  subject to random drug and alcohol tests  why then do we allow truck drivers to be  employed without similar restrictions  if a pilot walked on board a plane high  i'm pretty sure someone  would stop him from taking off and  potentially killing all on board  why would companies allow employees to  get behind the wheel of a truck  without some sort of check and balance  that they're fit and able to drive  driving in any vehicle comes with the  responsibility of following the rules of  the road  to prevent accidents companies that hire  drivers to haul thousands of pounds of  cargo  need to ensure that their drivers also  take the proper  precautions while on the road no more  recklessness  no more ghost bikes thank you  you know i'm sorry to say i've been  involved with way too many of these and  as angela said you know no more ghost  spikes and  a lot of people remember it and see it  but  you have a preconceived idea of what you  think you're going to want to say and  then you listen to these people and you  listen to the  the hurt and the positive things that  the group is doing and the  the horrific things and that people be  left with so  that kind of just goes out the window of  what you had preconceived and  you know donna i learned something from  donna that i'd never thought of when we  were doing the  the memorial she she made a comment and  i'm sure i won't get it right but i'll  get the idea across that  you know when we lose a loved one they  die twice  the first time when we physically lose  them  and then the last time we speak their  name  and with ghostbike and all these people  around here  we're not going to stop speaking their  names we're going to set these white  bikes around  people are going to ask which they do  what their names were and we're going to  we're going to speak their names  and those that came before them um  i'm not going to bring that up right no  no i guess i will i mean matthew hunt  cara  dr cabane there's there's quite a few  that we've lost before that we will  continue speaking their names and  setting their bikes and  and these bikes for anybody watching a  lot of people ask quite often you know  what is a ghost bike and it's nothing  more  myself and ghost spike i see steve over  here and pablo and the rest of us that  have  that took this on we're a supporting  role these people for these people you  just saw that are doing the hard work in  the legislature  trying to go about putting their lives  back together we're gonna set these  bikes and continue doing it to remind  people  what's happened before what we can do to  avoid it again  and hopefully to start that conversation  and keep the conversation going with  with your kids with your family members  with your coworkers  to think  none of us will dare call and it wasn't  an accident somebody made a really bad  choice  when they should have knocked up behind  the wheel just like every one of us  hopefully  the people that are watching this make  that decision  make the right decision to avoid  anything make sure something bad doesn't  happen  put that phone down if it rings while  you are driving and if you have a  drinker  or two there's no excuse grab an uber  call a friend  and let's avoid this and as angela said  let's not have any more ghost bikes  i'd like to thank all of you for coming  out  gonna wrap it up thank you thank you all  for being here
 

